        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 powder can be produced by inert-gas atomisation.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 HEA is applied as a coating to a Cu substrate.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spark plasma sintering can produce a dense AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 HEA microstructure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spark plasma sintering will ensure good adhesion between the HEA coating and Cu substrate.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 has been tested under reciprocating wear at 800 °C and 900 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "An atmospheric wear environment permits tribo-oxidation of the coating.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature wear forms a stable, spinel-like protective oxide film on the HEA surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide film mediates load transfer and protects both the HEA coating and the Cu substrate.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective oxide layer reduces wear depth.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective oxide layer reduces the coefficient of friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sintering promotes a strong metallurgical bond between AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 and Cu.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 exhibits a distinct reduction in wear depth at 800 °C and its highest reported wear resistance at 900 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "An AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5-coated Cu matrix will have lower wear depth than bare Cu under equivalent elevated-temperature conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5-coated Cu matrix will have a lower coefficient of friction than bare Cu under equivalent elevated-temperature conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The wear benefit is expected mainly at high temperatures where tribo-oxidation occurs.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional phases such as sigma phase could form in the coating and influence wear performance.",
